Description: PscoresPlus is an R package for summarising and interpreting treatment hierarchies from
    network meta-analysis (NMA) using extended P-scores. Extended P-scores create hierarchies that take 
    into account multiple outcomes and clinically important values (CIVs). It helps users explore how 
    rankings change when different CIVs are assumed, including sensitivity analysis to considering a range
    of CIVs. The package quantifies hierarchy stability using Precision of Treatment Hierarchy (POTH). 
    It provides the Average of P-scores over CIVs (APC) to summarise treatment performance across a range 
    of CIVs and multiple outcomes simultaneously. It also includes graphical tools to compare and visualize 
    treatment hierarchies across outcomes and CIV ranges.
